# Cookbook chapter template: the document documents/examples/orchard-and-field with Slots for each chapter of The
# Slow Autumn Kitchen. The book (its title, its author and its language), the layout of the opener and of a recipe and
# their labels are part of the template; the number and the title of the chapter, its subject and keywords, the number
# of its first page, the opening paragraphs, the plate and the recipes come in the data. A recipe has its id, title,
# yield, preparation and oven times and lead, and either an "ingredient_list", with the ingredients and the method
# side by side, or a "quantity_table", a numbered table of the quantities for two tins with the method below it in two
# columns. A row of the table has either one amount for each tin or one "shared" by both, in a cell that spans the two
# columns. The cook's notes with their drawing, the variations and a tip are optional. The paragraphs are Markdown.
# orchard-and-field.json has the sample data.
#
# A5 pages printed on both sides: Mirror margins gives the even pages the wide margin on the right, and the folios go
# on the outer edge with two Page overlay, one for the odd pages, with the title of the book, and one for the even
# ones, with the recipe in effect as a running head ({heading 2}). The chapter starts at the page in the data (Page
# numbering: restart, First number). The opener has a drop cap (Drop cap: 3), an illustration as a numbered Figure
# ("Plate 1.") and the list of recipes as a Table of contents of the Heading 2 level. Each recipe starts on a new page
# with its details on a shared baseline. The ingredients go in a List whose markers are a leaf drawn in SVG (Marker:
# image), with the method as a numbered List beside them, in a Grid. The cook's notes run around a small illustration
# (Side: right), the variations go in two Columns, and the quantity table has a numbered caption. The body text is IBM
# Plex Serif, justified with optimal line breaking and hyphenation (Language: en-GB).
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Page:
		Paper: A5
		Margin: 16mm 14mm 18mm 20mm
		Mirror margins: true
	Title: ${title} · Chapter ${chapter} of The Slow Autumn Kitchen
	Subject: <subject>
	Author: Hanna Brookes
	Keywords: <keywords>
	Language: en-GB
	Page overlay:
		Id: folio-odd
		Pages: odd
		Offset: auto 0 -11mm 0
		Style: folio
		Stack:
			Horizontal: right
			Gap: 10
			Item:
				Text: The Slow Autumn Kitchen
					Style: folio-title
			Item:
				# A value that starts with {page} would be the navigation {page}: the empty ${?_} in front, which no
				# data fills, makes the whole value text.
				Text: ${?_}{page}
					Style: folio-number
	Page overlay:
		Id: folio-even
		Pages: even
		Offset: auto 0 -11mm 0
		Style: folio
		Stack:
			Gap: 10
			Item:
				Text: ${?_}{page}
					Style: folio-number
			Item:
				Text: {heading 2}
					Style: folio-title
	Section:
		Id: chapter
		Page numbering: restart
		First number: <first_page>
		Block:
			Id: opener
			Text: Chapter ${chapter}
				Style: chapter-number
			Heading 1:
				Text: <title>
			Paragraph: <intro>
				Style: intro
				Drop cap: 3
			Paragraph: <?intro_more>
				Style: intro-more
			Figure: {plate}
				Id: <id>
				Caption: <caption>
				Image: <image>
					Alt: <alt>
					Box:
						Width: 62%
			Text: In this chapter
				Style: list-label
			Table of contents:
				Id: recipes-toc
				Levels: 2 2
		Block: [recipes]
			Id: <id>
			Style: recipe
			Heading 2:
				Text: <title>
			Stack:
				Style: details
				Item:
					Text: <yield>
						Style: detail-main
				Item:
					Text: Prep ${prep}
						Style: detail
				Item:
					Text: Oven ${oven}
						Style: detail
			Paragraph: <lead>
				Style: lead
			# The ingredients and the method side by side.
			Grid: {?ingredient_list}
				Style: recipe-grid
				Area:
					Block:
						Style: ingredients
						Text: Ingredients
							Style: list-label
						List:
							Style: leaves
							List item: [ingredients]
								Text: <text>
				Area:
					Block:
						Text: Method
							Style: list-label
						List:
							Style: steps
							List item: [method]
								Paragraph: <text>
			# The quantities for each tin, with a cell that spans the two for a quantity shared by both, and the method
			# below in two columns.
			Figure: {?quantity_table}
				Id: ${id}-quantities
				Caption: <caption>
				Table:
					Style: quantities
					Header rows:
						Row:
							Cell: Ingredient
							Cell: [tins]
					Body rows:
						Row: [rows]
							Cell: <ingredient>
								Row header: true
							Cell: [?amounts]
							Cell: <?shared>
								Style: span-note
								Span: 1 2
			Text: {?quantity_table}Method
				Style: list-label
			Columns: {?quantity_table}
				Style: method-columns
				List:
					Style: steps
					List item: [method]
						Paragraph: <text>
			Heading 3: {?notes}
				Text: Cook’s notes
			Image: {?notes}<drawing>
				Style: side-drawing
				Side: right
			Paragraph: {?notes}[paragraphs]
			Block: {?variations}
				Style: variations
				Text: Variations
					Style: list-label
				Columns:
					Style: variation-columns
					Paragraph: [items]**${name}.** ${text}
			Block: {?tip}
				Style: tip
				Paragraph: **${title}** ${text}
